    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (modeled on `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws when the count reaches 100. Placed before `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` so a full day never persists a record. It counts by the same \"today\" stamp `BuildOwner` assigns to new owners.\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (checked exception) and **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** (responds 429) in `rest/escalation/`.\n3. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n4. Wired a `checkDailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`, under the `transaction` governance like the surrounding steps.\n\nSeed owners have a NULL `registration_date`, so today's count starts at 0 \u2014 the acceptance test's assumption (100 succeed, the 101st is rejected) holds. `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` and the full suite pass.",
